<title>SINGAPORE: San Teh 1996 net profit up 14.5 pct.</title>
<headline>San Teh 1996 net profit up 14.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			 17.48   vs    15.26</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)		    8.0    vs     8.0</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		 7.47   vs     6.88</p>
<p>    Group shr (fully diluted)     7.06   vs     6.48</p>
<p>    Turnover			   81.67   vs    70.78</p>
<p>    Other income incl intr	  2.29   vs     1.91</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		0.67   vs     0.45</p>
<p>    Operating pre-tax		18.42   vs    17.54</p>
<p>    Associates			  1.34   vs     0.50</p>
<p>    Tax				   1.74   vs     2.84</p>
<p>    Minorities		loss    0.54   vs     0.51 (gain)</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:		July 16</p>
<p>    Last day books open:	    July 3</p>
<p>Note - Rubber keypad maker San Teh Ltd said its 69.7 percent-owned Longyan cement plant had completed its first production line in January 1997 and was scheduled to start operation in May. But the plant was not expected to contribute to the group's earnings in 1997 as this would be its first year in business.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom(54-8703080)</p>
</text>
